---

<BlogArticleShell
  title="4K QC Video: How to Audit High-Definition Warehouse Footage | kakobuy-cn.com"
  description="Mastering the new 2026 4K QC video feature on Kakobuy. Learn what to look for in motion, how to spot texture flaws, and when to request a retake."
  canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
  headline="4K QC Video: The New Standard for Spreadsheet Verification in 2026"
  publishedISO={publishedISO}
  displayDate="20 May 2026"
  structuredKeywords={[
    'Kakobuy 4K QC video',
    'warehouse inspection video',
    'spotting reps flaws',
    'high definition QC',
    'video inspection guide',
  ]}
>
  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    This guide supports shoppers on the <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet</a></strong> directory at kakobuy-cn.com. Static photos can hide a lot. A clever angle or a bit of overexposure can mask a wonky swoosh or a poor leather texture. In 2026, <strong>Kakobuy</strong> introduced <strong>4K QC Videos</strong> as a standard service. This guide teaches you how to "read" these videos like a pro.
  </p>

  <h2>1. The "Light Test": Spotting Material Flaws</h2>
  <p>
    As the warehouse agent moves the item under the lights, watch for <strong>reflections</strong>. Genuine-grade leather has a specific "grain" that reacts to light differently than synthetic alternatives. 
  </p>

  <h2>2. The "Flex Test": Checking Construction</h2>
  <p>
    In the video, agents will often flex the sole or pull the stitching. This is your chance to see the <strong>structural integrity</strong> that a photo can't capture. Look for:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Glue stains that only appear when the material is stretched.</li>
    <li>Loose threads that "pop" during movement.</li>
    <li>Inconsistent padding thickness in <a href="/category/hoodies/">hoodies</a> and <a href="/category/jackets/">jackets</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Comparing with Spreadsheet "Stock" Videos</h2>
  <p>
    Many sellers now include videos in their <a href="/blog/yupoo-album-spreadsheet-kakobuy-intake/">Yupoo albums</a>. Always compare the seller's "studio video" with Kakobuy's "warehouse video." If the movement of the fabric looks stiffer in the warehouse, it's a sign of a lower-tier batch.
  </p>

  <h2>When to Request a Retake</h2>
  <p>
    If the video is blurry, too fast, or misses a key area (like the size tag or the inner lining), don't hesitate to use the "Message Agent" button. In 2026, QC is a <strong>dialogue</strong>, not a one-way street. See our <a href="/blog/kakobuy-spreadsheet-qc/">full QC guide</a> for more on rejection criteria.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Conclusion:</strong> 4K Video is the ultimate "anti-scam" tool. Take the 30 seconds to watch it carefully—it could save you from a very expensive disappointment.
  </p>
</BlogArticleShell>
